; TestBoardDrivetrainTeleop: test-board bring-up.
;   1. Clear the DRIVETRAIN and SCIENCE fault latches (the E-STOP itself is hardware: release
;      the button; software cannot clear it).
;   2. Exempt wheel 4's INA780B from fault protection (DRIVE4 only; the others stay checked).
;   3. Give SCIENCE the drivetrain's bounds: 13.6 V low, 35 V high, 100 A.
;   4. Power on the drivetrain, then science.
;
; Every command is R00:00:00: each one goes out the moment the previous one answers, so the
; whole sequence runs in milliseconds. Any command that fails stops the sequence there.
; The parameter changes are runtime only (not PRM_SAVE_FILE'd): a reboot restores the saved or
; default values.
R00:00:00 rp2350Deployment.fpManager.CLEAR_FAULT DRIVETRAIN
R00:00:00 rp2350Deployment.fpManager.CLEAR_FAULT SCIENCE
R00:00:00 rp2350Deployment.fpManager.EXEMPT_DRIVETRAIN_SENSOR_PRM_SET '{"DRIVE1": false, "DRIVE2": false, "DRIVE3": false, "DRIVE4": true, "DRIVE5": false, "DRIVE6": false}'
R00:00:00 rp2350Deployment.fpManager.SCIENCE_BOUNDS_PRM_SET '{"vbusFaultLow": 13.6, "vbusFaultHigh": 35.0, "currentFaultHigh": 100.0}'
R00:00:00 rp2350Deployment.subsystemManager.SET_DRIVETRAIN_POWER_STATE ON
R00:00:00 rp2350Deployment.subsystemManager.SET_SCIENCE_POWER_STATE ON
